---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import CallButton from '../components/CallButton.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE, HOURS_KNOWN } from '../lib/site';
---
<Page
  title="Water Damage Baytown TX: Service Area and ZIP Codes"
  description="Water damage and fire damage help across Baytown, TX ZIP codes 77520, 77521 and 77523. See the neighborhoods, local risks and emergency contacts."
  h1="Baytown, TX Service Area"
  h1Html="Baytown, TX <em>Service Area</em>"
  eyebrow="Where we help"
  sub="One city, covered properly: Baytown, Texas, across three ZIP codes. If you have water damage in Baytown, TX, or damage from a fire, the phone line is answered day and night."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Service Area', path: '/service-area/' }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="area">
        <div>
          <iframe
            class="map"
            title="Map of Baytown, Texas"
            loading="lazy"
            referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
            src="https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-95.105%2C29.675%2C-94.835%2C29.845&amp;layer=mapnik"
          ></iframe>
          <p class="source-note">Map of the Baytown area for reference. Map data &copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="area__head">
            <p class="k">ZIP codes covered</p>
            <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 6px">Baytown, TX</h2>
            <p>Calls from these three ZIP codes reach restoration crews that work in Baytown.</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="dotlist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
            <li><strong>77520</strong>: south and central Baytown, including the older parts of town and the bayfront</li>
            <li><strong>77521</strong>: central and north Baytown, including the Garth Road corridor toward Interstate 10</li>
            <li><strong>77523</strong>: the east side across Cedar Bayou, largely in Chambers County</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <CallButton label="Call {phone}" location="service-area" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-light">
    <div class="wrap article-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Water damage in Baytown, TX: who can get help</h2>
        <p>
          Any home in the three Baytown ZIP codes. The area is kept small on purpose, so the restoration crews you talk to are ones that actually work in Baytown and know its housing, its humidity and its storm seasons.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you live just outside these ZIP codes, you are welcome to call and ask. Whether a company can come out depends on who is available that day, and we would sooner tell you that than promise coverage we cannot confirm.
        </p>

        <h2>Parts of Baytown the line covers</h2>
        <p>
          Baytown grew out of three oil-boom towns, Goose Creek, Pelly and Baytown, which merged into one city in 1948. That history still shows in the housing, and housing age has a lot to do with the kind of water damage a home is prone to.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Old Baytown, Goose Creek and Pelly.</strong> The streets around Texas Avenue and south toward the bay hold some of the oldest houses in the city. Older plumbing, original cast iron drains and pier-and-beam floors are common, so slow leaks under the house and aging supply lines are typical risks.</li>
          <li><strong>Wooster.</strong> A west-side area that was once its own community before becoming part of Baytown. Low-lying streets close to the bay have dealt with storm surge and tidal flooding.</li>
          <li><strong>The Garth Road corridor and north Baytown.</strong> Newer subdivisions on slab foundations toward Interstate 10. Typical problems in homes like these are water heater failures, supply line breaks, air conditioner drain leaks and slab leaks.</li>
          <li><strong>Cedar Bayou and the east side.</strong> Homes on both sides of Cedar Bayou, extending into Chambers County. Heavy rain and bayou flooding are the usual concerns.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Local landmarks, for orientation</h2>
        <p>
          If you are new to town, the area we cover runs roughly from the Fred Hartman Bridge and the Houston Ship Channel in the south, past Lee College and the Texas Avenue district, up Garth Road to Interstate 10, and east across Cedar Bayou. The Baytown Nature Center, on the peninsula between Burnet Bay and Scott Bay, sits on the site of the former Brownwood subdivision, a neighborhood that was abandoned after repeated flooding. It is a useful reminder of how much the water shapes life here.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Baytown homes get water damage</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Water on three sides.</strong> The San Jacinto River, Galveston Bay and Cedar Bayou border the city, and Goose Creek runs through it.</li>
          <li><strong>Hurricane season.</strong> June through November brings the risk of tropical rain and storm surge. Hurricane Ike in 2008 and Hurricane Harvey in 2017 both left lasting damage in Baytown.</li>
          <li><strong>Humidity and heat.</strong> Air conditioners run most of the year, wet materials dry slowly, and mold gets started quickly.</li>
          <li><strong>The occasional hard freeze.</strong> Rare, but houses here are not built for it. The February 2021 freeze broke pipes across the region.</li>
          <li><strong>Slab foundations on clay soil.</strong> Plumbing under a slab is hard to see and hard to reach when it leaks.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We cover each of these in depth: <a href="/water-damage-restoration-baytown-tx/">water damage restoration</a>, <a href="/flood-storm-water-cleanup-baytown/">flood and storm cleanup</a>, <a href="/burst-pipe-water-damage-baytown/">burst pipes and leaks</a>, <a href="/mold-after-water-damage-baytown/">mold after water damage</a> and <a href="/fire-smoke-damage-restoration-baytown-tx/">fire and smoke damage</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Useful local contacts in an emergency</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Fire, injury or immediate danger:</strong> call 911.</li>
          <li><strong>Gas smell:</strong> leave the house and call your gas utility or 911 from outside.</li>
          <li><strong>Downed power lines or wet electrical equipment:</strong> stay away and contact your electric utility.</li>
          <li><strong>Water main breaks, street flooding and storm information:</strong> the <a href="https://www.baytown.org/" rel="noopener">City of Baytown</a> website lists city departments and emergency management updates.</li>
          <li><strong>Forecasts and flood warnings:</strong> the <a href="https://www.weather.gov/hgx/" rel="noopener">National Weather Service Houston/Galveston office</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Call">
        <div class="side-box">
          <h2>In 77520, 77521 or 77523?</h2>
          <p>Call any time, day or night, to get a restoration crew scheduled for your part of Baytown.</p>
          <CallButton label="Call {phone}" location="sidebar" />
        </div>
        <div class="side-box side-box--light">
          {HOURS_KNOWN ? <><h2>Phone hours</h2><p>Answered day and night</p></> : <h2>Before you call</h2>}
          <p style="margin:0"><a href="/how-it-works/">See what happens when you call</a></p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand heading="Damage in <em>Baytown?</em>" text="The line is answered day and night. Call to get a local restoration crew scheduled for your ZIP code." label="Call {phone}" />
</Page>
